  "description": "The PD 2 features a low stand-over height frame for easier climbing in and out. Its lightweight X6 series alloy frame features an internal headset and internal cable routing, which keep everything neatly tucked out of the way. It comes standard with an upgraded 2x9 drive train, versatile and capable of handling a wide variety of terrain. It glides along on strong U-26 double-wall rims, stainless steel spokes and Kenda Kwick Seven.5 tires with reflective sidewalls for increased safety. The Suntour XCT-30, 100mm travel fork features a hydraulic lockout, which deactivates the up and down motion associated with suspension, thereby reducing pedaling energy loss when needed.\nHaro PD2 27.5\" X6 alloy frame\nSR XCT-30 HLO fork, 100mm\nAltus MT210-2 36/22T crankset\nAlivio M4000 2x9 derailleurs\nPivit Adjustable-rise stem 105mm\nComfort grips w/ integrated Bar-Ends\nWTB Comfort Sport saddle\nWeinmann U-26 rims w/ Stainless spokes\nKenda Kwick Seven 2.0\" tires w/ reflective stripes\nPromax disc brakes\nRear rack, Water-Bottle cage & Kickstand",
